Z||000000||falconhulk||10-24-2001||11:00 AM||||Anyone have a 2.8 puting out in the nieghboorhodd of 200hp? If so how much did it cost and can you list the mods?  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fiero_24||10-24-2001||11:14 AM||||You can go to my site and look at my V6 page.  For everything I did including a whole bunch of new parts I was under $3K (I am puting in the engine myself to save money).  I am not sure how much HP I will have, but I am adding headers and a Borla exhaust in a few months too.<P>edit:<P>The new motor was built with a Performance Rebuild that includes:<BR>TRW power forged pistons, moly rings, High flow oil pump, complete gasket and seal set, Timing chain and sproket, Crane cam and lifter set, Hi-Po steel retainers, all new galley and freeze plugs, cam, rod, and main bearings. <P>Here is a list of the other new parts:<P>1. New Starter <BR>2. New alternator<BR>3. Bosch 4 prong platnum plugs<BR>4. New water pump <BR>5. Performance Valve job <BR>6. New O2 Sensor<BR>7. New Cold Start Injector Switch<BR>8. Reman Distributor<BR>9. New Spark Plug wires<BR>10. New Oil Pan<BR>11. All New Gaskets<BR>12. New oil pick up tibe w/screen<P>I had the heads bowl ported and a 3 way valve job.  the engine was only bored 30 over.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg">  <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT<p>[This message has been edited by Fiero_24 (edited 10-24-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||TRiAD||10-24-2001||11:28 AM||||As soon as my GT gets here. I will be working on an Eaton Supercharger package that will be sufficiently over 200hp. <P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg">  <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I><p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 10-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||falconhulk||10-24-2001||12:45 PM||||Yeah Triad I am counting on that but just in case I was looking in to naturally aspirated fun.  I am goinh to try to hold out .......dont let us down||||reg||1
Z||000004||chester||10-24-2001||01:02 PM||||I just rebuilt my V6 this spring. <BR>Running a 1988 Formula drivetrain. 2.8/Getrag combo with the following mods;<P>Bored .030 over.<BR>Crane 2030 cam<BR>TRW forged pistons (9.5:1)<BR>Heads shaved .020 mild port/polish<BR>ARP Racing hardware throughout<BR>SS valves<BR>Crane springs/retainers/locks/pushrods<BR>Comp Cams 1:1.6 roller tip rockers.<BR>Cloyes true double roller timing chain.<BR>High volume oil pump<BR>Windage tray<BR>FULL BALANCE! I run polly motor mounts with NO vibration!<BR>Adjustable fuel pressure regulator with guage.<BR>Magnacore 10MM racing wires<BR>19# Accel injectors<BR>Bored throttle body and plenum<BR>Accel Super Coil<BR>Custom headers<BR>Power pully kit<BR>Hypertech Stage III chip.<BR>WCF Flowmaster<BR>2 1/4" exhaust<BR>FieroShop Cold air induction with K&N cone filter.<BR>MSD 6AL<BR>Centerforce dual friction clutch and Dunlop SP9000 245/40/17's on the rear to put it all to the ground. <P>Here's a pic;<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine_pic.jpg"> <BR> <P>I also have a high volume fuel pump ready to go just haven't had the time to put it in.<P>Future expansions are T3/T4? Garret turbo<BR>Accel DFI programmable ECM (on the way!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<BR>Small shot of NOS (Like the Venom 2000 series )<P>Desktop dyno showed it at 210.  We will see.  Once I install the DFI I'm going to have it dyno tuned so I'll know for sure.<P>Rob D<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">   <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
Z||000005||falconhulk||10-24-2001||01:10 PM||||chester<BR>Let us know what you get from that.  Thats a pretty extensive list.  How much $$$$ did you sink in to it?||||reg||1
Z||000006||chester||10-24-2001||01:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by falconhulk:<BR><B>chester<BR>Let us know what you get from that.  That's a pretty extensive list.  How much $$$$ did you sink in to it?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Roughly $3000 counting headers, exhaust and clutch. Parts only. No labor, machine work costs or cost of ECM.<P>Rob D.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fiero_24||10-24-2001||02:16 PM||||Chester, Nice setup!  I have a lot of the same stuff as you as you, minus a few extra's.  I ran out of money replacing sensors and sending units to go on the new motor.  How much HP do you have out of yours?  I also had my motor balanced, I heard it free's up a little extra HP.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg">  <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT<p>[This message has been edited by Fiero_24 (edited 10-24-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000008||chester||10-24-2001||02:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero_24:<BR><B>Chester, Nice setup!  I have a lot of the same stuff as you as you, minus a few extra's.  I ran out of money replacing sensors and sending units to go on the new motor.  How much HP do you have out of yours?  I also had my motor balanced, I heard it free's up a little extra HP.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks!  I don't have actual HP figures yet.  I have the Accel DFI on the way as we speak  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> .  As soon as it gets here I'm going to install it and have it dyno tuned.  Then I'll know for sure.  Hopefully within a couple of weeks.<P>Rob D.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fiero_24||10-24-2001||07:34 PM||||Chester, keep me informed when you have the HP.  I am interested to see what I am pushing, but first I have to finish my swap (darn front cradle bolts slowed me down).  I may be adding NOS this spring after it is broken in.<P>Craig<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||10
Z||000010||88formula||10-24-2001||09:11 PM||||Hey Chester! I ran your engine combination through Dyno2000 and I got 186 horsepower @ 5500 rpm and 203-ft. lbs. of torque @ 4000 rpm. I then ran this through Dragstrip2000 and got 0-60 in 6.25 seconds and the quarter mile in 14.5 seconds @ 93.6 mph.<P>I'm thinking of bringing my Formula to New England Dragway Saturday. Do you want to meet me there by any chance?<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||sluppy123||10-24-2001||10:54 PM||||A well built turbo-charged, non-intercooled 2.8 running 6-7 psi boost will get you over 200hp. By a kit for $3k+ or build your own for around $1k.<P>------------------<BR>-Brian, Toolmaker<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>87' GT-Galaxy silver mettalic, Turbo Charged, Modified 2.8- 235 HP w/ 7 psi Boost, Eibach Sport springs, RSM side scoops, Mr Mikes leather, 17" Mille Miglia's. <BR>                <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1711832&a=12781563&p=54316496&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
